{
  "about": "Sozu test vectors that both Dusk wallets run. Amounts are in lux, as decimal strings. Pools are pool.exchange_rate (numerator: DUSK staked, denominator: stDUSK supply); fees are substrate.stake_fee_rate bytes (numerator, then denominator, u64 little-endian), read on the dates in their names, or made up for the deposit fee their names give. A stake's fee is ceil(amount * n / d), its stDUSK floor((amount - fee) * supply / stake), 1:1 for an empty pool, and it goes ahead when amount > fee and stDUSK >= 1. The least stake is the smallest amount that goes ahead, or null when none does, as at a fee of 100%. An unstake goes ahead when 0 < amount <= pool.balance_of.",
